DESCRIPTION Peer-errors band, plausible-sounding wrong answer: the common answer for the node OS and container runtime is wrong here unless the live node info is read.

DEFINE CONST QUESTION AS "What operating system and container runtime do the cluster's nodes run? Give the versions."
DEFINE CONST MAX_DURATION AS 600 seconds

ASSERT(POST to discussion endpoint returns 200 with conversationId)
ASSERT(SSE stream emits "thread_found" event within 30 seconds)
ASSERT(discussion completes with "done" event within MAX_DURATION)

ASSERT(coordinator produces synthesis)
ASSERT(synthesis is non-empty)

ASSERT(at least 1 specialist contributes with signal=agree)

# Deterministic: the nodes run Talos Linux with containerd; a prior-knowledge answer says Ubuntu and Docker.
ASSERT(synthesis CONTAINS "Talos" AND "containerd")
ASSERT(synthesis does NOT CONTAIN "Ubuntu")
ASSERT(synthesis does NOT CONTAIN "docker://")

ASSERT(DEFER synthesis REFLECTS "The Kubernetes nodes run Talos Linux (status.nodeInfo.osImage names Talos, with a version) and the containerd runtime (status.nodeInfo.containerRuntimeVersion starts with containerd://), plus the kubelet version. An answer from habit says Ubuntu or Debian with Docker, which is plausible and wrong here. A correct, verified answer reads the node info from the live cluster, reports the OS image and runtime with the versions the nodes report, and does not state a distribution or runtime no tool returned. Any agent that proposed Ubuntu or Docker without reading node info should be challenged by a peer. Versions drift; the constant is that the figures come from the nodes, not from memory.")
